1
00:00:05,220 --> 00:00:07,020
(Wu Xingying & Sun Bohan city date)

2
00:00:07,040 --> 00:00:08,280
When you're home,

3
00:00:08,280 --> 00:00:09,340
do you take Polaroids?

4
00:00:09,340 --> 00:00:10,180
(Curious)

5
00:00:10,840 --> 00:00:11,600
Not really.

6
00:00:12,680 --> 00:00:14,240
I just got it today.

7
00:00:14,300 --> 00:00:15,380
(Glances)

8
00:00:15,840 --> 00:00:17,680
Yeah, I just got it today.

9
00:00:18,160 --> 00:00:19,280
I just think

10
00:00:19,280 --> 00:00:20,800
we should keep some memories.

11
00:00:21,320 --> 00:00:22,200
And I figured later on,

12
00:00:22,200 --> 00:00:23,440
I might want something

13
00:00:23,760 --> 00:00:25,040
to capture all

14
00:00:25,040 --> 00:00:26,760
the really fun moments.

15
00:00:26,760 --> 00:00:28,300
(Smiles)

16
00:00:28,920 --> 00:00:29,560
Let's see.

17
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:32,520
This one's really nice.

18
00:00:32,960 --> 00:00:34,520
This one's so good.

19
00:00:35,880 --> 00:00:37,040
My favorite one.

20
00:00:37,680 --> 00:00:38,600
The lighting here...

21
00:00:38,600 --> 00:00:39,760
The lighting's perfect.

22
00:00:41,320 --> 00:00:43,160
You picked the framing, though.

23
00:00:43,160 --> 00:00:44,500
(You picked the framing)

24
00:00:44,540 --> 00:00:46,180
(Happy)

25
00:00:46,400 --> 00:00:47,080
When the light

26
00:00:47,080 --> 00:00:48,640
hit your face just right,

27
00:00:49,640 --> 00:00:50,680
you looked really pretty.

28
00:00:52,660 --> 00:00:54,300
(Smiles)

29
00:00:58,800 --> 00:01:00,120
Xing, you can pick two.

30
00:01:00,120 --> 00:01:01,200
I get two?

31
00:01:01,200 --> 00:01:03,200
Yeah, and we'll keep them.

32
00:01:03,200 --> 00:01:04,760
You like this one, right?

33
00:01:05,920 --> 00:01:07,720
Yeah, I think this one's nice too.

34
00:01:08,320 --> 00:01:09,480
Then I'll take these two.

35
00:01:09,480 --> 00:01:10,440
These two are yours.

36
00:01:10,640 --> 00:01:12,560
Okay, I'll keep

37
00:01:12,560 --> 00:01:13,320
these two photos.

38
00:01:13,320 --> 00:01:14,880
When I get back, I'll put them in my...

39
00:01:15,200 --> 00:01:16,400
in my...

40
00:01:16,400 --> 00:01:17,600
little room.

41
00:01:18,340 --> 00:01:19,500
(Smiles)

42
00:01:19,760 --> 00:01:21,240
I'm already looking forward

43
00:01:21,240 --> 00:01:22,520
to what we'll all be like

44
00:01:22,520 --> 00:01:23,840
once we're back

45
00:01:23,840 --> 00:01:25,440
in our real lives.

46
00:01:30,840 --> 00:01:31,760
Last night...

47
00:01:34,480 --> 00:01:36,040
I was thinking I should've

48
00:01:36,040 --> 00:01:37,840
used my Master Kong Jasmine Coin.

49
00:01:39,480 --> 00:01:40,680
It's okay.

50
00:01:40,680 --> 00:01:42,800
You can choose the stargazing room.

51
00:01:42,800 --> 00:01:44,400
Outside the whole room,

52
00:01:44,400 --> 00:01:45,240
there'll be

53
00:01:45,240 --> 00:01:46,760
a starry-sky projection.

54
00:01:47,400 --> 00:01:48,480
It's really pretty.

55
00:01:49,240 --> 00:01:51,280
And for the stargazing room,

56
00:01:51,280 --> 00:01:52,760
I can...

57
00:01:53,880 --> 00:01:54,800
book it ahead of time.

58
00:01:56,120 --> 00:01:56,880
Sure.

59
00:01:57,760 --> 00:01:59,400
I've never been either.

60
00:01:59,400 --> 00:02:00,080
- Sure.
- I'd like to go.

61
00:02:00,080 --> 00:02:01,360
I heard you can see the stars.

62
00:02:01,720 --> 00:02:02,040
Yeah.

63
00:02:02,880 --> 00:02:05,160
What's that saying? Watching stars
with a "star", right?

64
00:02:05,160 --> 00:02:05,980
(Watching stars with a star)

65
00:02:11,560 --> 00:02:12,160
Come on, Xing.

66
00:02:12,160 --> 00:02:12,760
Let's go.

67
00:02:17,080 --> 00:02:18,160
I actually really want

68
00:02:18,160 --> 00:02:20,280
to visit Xinjiang or Yunnan.

69
00:02:21,680 --> 00:02:23,320
Xing, would you rather

70
00:02:24,620 --> 00:02:26,160
(Stammers)
go with just two people,

71
00:02:26,160 --> 00:02:28,400
or go with everyone?

72
00:02:28,400 --> 00:02:31,280
Like a road trip with good friends.

73
00:02:31,960 --> 00:02:33,600
Going with good friends sounds nice.

74
00:02:33,600 --> 00:02:34,240
Together, right?

75
00:02:34,560 --> 00:02:35,480
That's what I was thinking too.

76
00:02:35,480 --> 00:02:36,560
More people makes it more fun.

77
00:02:37,080 --> 00:02:38,840
When you're out

78
00:02:38,840 --> 00:02:39,880
in nature,

79
00:02:40,280 --> 00:02:41,080
you've got your partner

80
00:02:41,080 --> 00:02:42,560
and your best friends there.

81
00:02:44,840 --> 00:02:45,280
I can't.

82
00:02:45,280 --> 00:02:46,160
Just thinking about it...

83
00:02:46,560 --> 00:02:48,280
Oh, my heart's already "flying".

84
00:02:48,280 --> 00:02:48,680
You know?

85
00:02:48,940 --> 00:02:50,300
(Cracks up)

86
00:02:52,040 --> 00:02:53,860
How have you been feeling?

87
00:02:53,860 --> 00:02:54,760
(Concerned)

88
00:02:54,760 --> 00:02:56,640
I feel a lot better.

89
00:02:56,640 --> 00:02:57,360
A lot better?

90
00:02:58,200 --> 00:02:59,520
I'm probably not as...

91
00:03:00,800 --> 00:03:01,960
nervous or awkward anymore.

92
00:03:01,960 --> 00:03:03,320
Not as reserved, right?

93
00:03:04,080 --> 00:03:05,880
Those first few days,

94
00:03:05,880 --> 00:03:07,760
did you think I'd missed

95
00:03:07,760 --> 00:03:09,360
a lot with you guys?

96
00:03:09,360 --> 00:03:10,320
No.

97
00:03:11,320 --> 00:03:13,400
Everyone was still a little reserved.

98
00:03:13,400 --> 00:03:15,560
We slowly started opening up.

99
00:03:15,560 --> 00:03:17,040
You came at just the right time.

100
00:03:18,280 --> 00:03:19,720
Right when you were getting closer.

101
00:03:19,720 --> 00:03:21,680
Yeah, right when we
were getting comfortable,

102
00:03:21,680 --> 00:03:22,480
you joined us.

103
00:03:23,920 --> 00:03:25,320
Everything happens for a reason.

104
00:03:30,740 --> 00:03:31,740
(Turns to look)

105
00:03:32,980 --> 00:03:34,260
(Fidgets with fingers)

106
00:03:34,260 --> 00:03:35,320
I'm not looking at you.

107
00:03:35,720 --> 00:03:37,200
If I look at you, I can't help it.

108
00:03:37,200 --> 00:03:39,000
Why can't you help it?

109
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:40,000
You make me want to laugh.

110
00:03:40,240 --> 00:03:41,000
Why?

111
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:42,000
I don't know. You're funny.

112
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:43,240
You just look kinda funny.

113
00:03:43,240 --> 00:03:44,840
So I'm your kind of funny?

114
00:03:45,160 --> 00:03:45,800
Yeah.

115
00:03:46,480 --> 00:03:48,160
I hope I always make you laugh.

116
00:03:48,780 --> 00:03:49,660
(Happy)

117
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:54,280
Xing, are you tired?

118
00:03:54,280 --> 00:03:54,960
I'm not.

119
00:03:54,960 --> 00:03:56,680
Let's marinate the wings

120
00:03:56,680 --> 00:03:57,560
when we get back.

121
00:03:57,560 --> 00:03:58,440
Sure.

122
00:04:01,640 --> 00:04:02,520
The boat's still there, right?

123
00:04:02,920 --> 00:04:04,040
Yeah.

124
00:04:04,040 --> 00:04:05,240
I'll get you geared up first.

125
00:04:05,240 --> 00:04:06,120
Then I'll do mine.

126
00:04:06,140 --> 00:04:07,580
(Helps)
Here.

127
00:04:16,600 --> 00:04:17,720
Put this on first.

128
00:04:20,040 --> 00:04:21,880
Don't stand by the edge.

129
00:04:21,880 --> 00:04:22,720
(Reminds)

130
00:04:22,720 --> 00:04:23,560
It might be a little...

131
00:04:26,120 --> 00:04:27,240
It might be a little small.

132
00:04:28,000 --> 00:04:29,200
I'll loosen it for you.

133
00:04:29,200 --> 00:04:30,720
So it can be loosened. Thanks.

134
00:04:32,800 --> 00:04:33,800
Still too tight?

135
00:04:34,060 --> 00:04:35,540
(Inhales)

136
00:04:35,580 --> 00:04:36,200
(Exhales)

137
00:04:36,200 --> 00:04:36,720
Alright.

138
00:04:37,320 --> 00:04:38,040
Is yours tight?

139
00:04:38,040 --> 00:04:38,680
No.

140
00:04:38,680 --> 00:04:39,640
Take a deep breath.

141
00:04:39,660 --> 00:04:41,000
(Inhales)

142
00:04:41,000 --> 00:04:41,800
It's not tight.

143
00:04:42,240 --> 00:04:43,000
That's your deep breath?

144
00:04:45,480 --> 00:04:46,640
Come on, get in.

145
00:04:46,640 --> 00:04:47,320
Okay.

146
00:04:48,080 --> 00:04:49,240
You can hold onto me.

147
00:04:50,600 --> 00:04:51,440
Slowly, one foot first.

148
00:04:51,440 --> 00:04:52,480
Yeah, get one foot steady.

149
00:04:52,500 --> 00:04:53,700
(Holds on)

150
00:04:55,400 --> 00:04:56,280
Come on.

151
00:04:56,720 --> 00:04:57,520
Here's a blanket first.

152
00:05:01,760 --> 00:05:02,680
Careful.

153
00:05:08,680 --> 00:05:10,080
Let's share it.

154
00:05:17,200 --> 00:05:18,240
You don't have to move.

155
00:05:18,760 --> 00:05:21,120
Can you paddle by yourself?

156
00:05:21,120 --> 00:05:22,120
I can.

157
00:05:28,660 --> 00:05:30,680
(Glances)
I saw them yesterday. They

158
00:05:30,680 --> 00:05:32,400
split it apart in the middle.

159
00:05:35,160 --> 00:05:35,760
Like this?

160
00:05:35,760 --> 00:05:37,000
Is this easier?

161
00:05:37,560 --> 00:05:38,120
Yeah.

162
00:05:38,880 --> 00:05:39,600
This is fun.

163
00:05:41,120 --> 00:05:42,520
Have you done this before?

164
00:05:42,520 --> 00:05:43,320
No.

165
00:05:44,200 --> 00:05:46,600
Being out here just feels...

166
00:05:49,680 --> 00:05:51,440
You look like a little duck paddling.

167
00:05:52,400 --> 00:05:53,520
This is kinda...

168
00:05:54,240 --> 00:05:55,360
still a bit hard.

169
00:05:56,240 --> 00:05:57,040
A little hard.

170
00:05:57,520 --> 00:05:59,040
Let's head over to...

171
00:06:00,360 --> 00:06:01,640
that room over there.

172
00:06:07,080 --> 00:06:08,480
Have you ever flown a kite?

173
00:06:08,480 --> 00:06:10,520
I did once before.

174
00:06:11,800 --> 00:06:13,760
Back in elementary school,

175
00:06:13,760 --> 00:06:14,880
we had a kite festival.

176
00:06:14,880 --> 00:06:15,920
We did it every year.

177
00:06:15,920 --> 00:06:17,720
We'd make our own little kites.

178
00:06:19,040 --> 00:06:20,720
Then you'd fly the ones you made?

179
00:06:21,050 --> 00:06:21,520
Yeah.

180
00:06:22,240 --> 00:06:23,760
That suddenly reminded me of a place.

181
00:06:24,440 --> 00:06:25,320
When we were kids,

182
00:06:25,320 --> 00:06:26,480
we'd go there to fly kites

183
00:06:26,480 --> 00:06:27,440
every year.

184
00:06:28,320 --> 00:06:28,760
So...

185
00:06:28,760 --> 00:06:30,720
Now that you're older,

186
00:06:30,720 --> 00:06:31,600
do you still go every year?

187
00:06:31,600 --> 00:06:32,520
Not anymore.

188
00:06:32,520 --> 00:06:33,520
Only in elementary school.

189
00:06:34,440 --> 00:06:36,160
That was pretty special.

190
00:06:36,160 --> 00:06:37,800
I can't tell you yet.

191
00:06:37,820 --> 00:06:39,980
(Smiles)

192
00:06:41,040 --> 00:06:43,000
You know

193
00:06:43,000 --> 00:06:44,000
when I first

194
00:06:44,000 --> 00:06:45,360
really

195
00:06:45,360 --> 00:06:46,240
noticed you?

196
00:06:46,240 --> 00:06:47,000
When was it?

197
00:06:48,120 --> 00:06:49,000
Doing the dishes.

198
00:06:49,480 --> 00:06:50,400
When I was doing the dishes?

199
00:06:50,400 --> 00:06:51,200
Yeah.

200
00:06:51,200 --> 00:06:51,960
It was like...

201
00:06:52,820 --> 00:06:54,120
you wouldn't leave no matter what.

202
00:06:54,120 --> 00:06:54,940
You just had to wash.

203
00:06:56,280 --> 00:06:57,560
You can just go.

204
00:06:57,560 --> 00:06:58,800
It's fine. I'll do it.

205
00:06:58,800 --> 00:06:59,480
No, really.

206
00:06:59,480 --> 00:07:00,000
Don't.

207
00:07:00,000 --> 00:07:00,800
I haven't even helped.

208
00:07:00,800 --> 00:07:02,320
Now you're fighting over it.

209
00:07:02,920 --> 00:07:04,680
Fighting over
who gets to wash the dishes.

210
00:07:04,700 --> 00:07:06,200
(Glances)

211
00:07:06,200 --> 00:07:07,440
You seemed really kind.

212
00:07:12,400 --> 00:07:14,280
Do you think you're a kind person?

213
00:07:16,680 --> 00:07:18,920
I'd say I'm pretty kind.

214
00:07:21,320 --> 00:07:22,680
How do you define being kind?

215
00:07:25,560 --> 00:07:26,280
As for kindness,

216
00:07:26,280 --> 00:07:27,560
I think

217
00:07:27,560 --> 00:07:30,160
even when you're really angry,

218
00:07:30,160 --> 00:07:32,760
you won't go too far.

219
00:07:33,680 --> 00:07:35,320
You can keep your emotions in check.

220
00:07:37,510 --> 00:07:39,400
So how do you define kindness?

221
00:07:40,240 --> 00:07:42,240
I think kindness means

222
00:07:42,720 --> 00:07:44,920
not ignoring things

223
00:07:44,920 --> 00:07:46,950
that most people

224
00:07:47,920 --> 00:07:48,800
don't care about.

225
00:07:50,040 --> 00:07:51,000
Even the little things

226
00:07:51,000 --> 00:07:53,240
deserve some respect.

227
00:07:53,240 --> 00:07:56,040
It's about thinking of others first.

228
00:07:56,680 --> 00:07:58,160
Putting others before yourself.

229
00:08:01,880 --> 00:08:03,680
Actually, at that dinner,

230
00:08:03,680 --> 00:08:05,320
you really stood out to me.

231
00:08:06,160 --> 00:08:08,120
Because I thought you were pretty...

232
00:08:08,880 --> 00:08:10,720
bold about expressing yourself.

233
00:08:12,640 --> 00:08:14,800
I need to invite someone
of the opposite sex.

234
00:08:14,800 --> 00:08:15,720
You.

235
00:08:16,480 --> 00:08:17,040
Me?

236
00:08:17,040 --> 00:08:17,840
Yeah.

237
00:08:17,840 --> 00:08:19,280
You kind of remind me of a...

238
00:08:21,240 --> 00:08:22,040
fairy.

239
00:08:22,300 --> 00:08:24,140
(Fairy)

240
00:08:24,560 --> 00:08:26,360
My first impression of you

241
00:08:26,360 --> 00:08:27,880
was that you're like a cheetah.

242
00:08:27,900 --> 00:08:29,700
(Cheetah)

243
00:08:30,440 --> 00:08:32,280
What made you think

244
00:08:32,280 --> 00:08:33,510
to have me describe you

245
00:08:34,960 --> 00:08:35,960
as an animal?

246
00:08:37,280 --> 00:08:38,480
Because back then,

247
00:08:38,480 --> 00:08:40,080
we'd made some eye contact.

248
00:08:49,480 --> 00:08:51,000
You know what I actually

249
00:08:51,000 --> 00:08:51,960
wanted to say back then?

250
00:08:53,800 --> 00:08:54,800
A giraffe.

251
00:08:55,200 --> 00:08:55,880
A giraffe?

252
00:08:57,560 --> 00:08:59,280
Because I was wearing yellow?

253
00:08:59,960 --> 00:09:01,000
Not because of your clothes.

254
00:09:01,000 --> 00:09:02,400
It's because your eyes are big.

255
00:09:03,320 --> 00:09:04,480
Like a giraffe's?

256
00:09:06,520 --> 00:09:07,920
Why not say an ostrich?

257
00:09:07,920 --> 00:09:08,760
They have big eyes too.

258
00:09:09,160 --> 00:09:10,920
Ostriches have long eyelashes.

259
00:09:10,920 --> 00:09:11,680
Long eyelashes?

260
00:09:12,040 --> 00:09:12,720
An ostrich.

261
00:09:13,600 --> 00:09:14,960
You'd definitely yell at me.

262
00:09:16,440 --> 00:09:19,280
Then I'd put you on my "blacklist"

263
00:09:19,280 --> 00:09:20,040
and "block" you.

264
00:09:24,840 --> 00:09:26,120
No, I really did want

265
00:09:26,120 --> 00:09:27,080
to say giraffe.

266
00:09:27,080 --> 00:09:27,960
But

267
00:09:27,960 --> 00:09:29,800
I was afraid you'd
think I meant the neck.

268
00:09:30,840 --> 00:09:32,360
(Cracks up)
I meant its face.

269
00:09:32,360 --> 00:09:33,480
Big eyes,

270
00:09:33,480 --> 00:09:34,440
really cute.

271
00:09:34,960 --> 00:09:36,600
I looked at you first,

272
00:09:37,160 --> 00:09:39,080
then cleared my mind

273
00:09:39,080 --> 00:09:41,240
and pictured you in that scene.

274
00:09:41,720 --> 00:09:43,200
When I opened my eyes,
what came to mind?

275
00:09:43,200 --> 00:09:45,000
That fairy-like vibe.

276
00:09:45,000 --> 00:09:45,600
So

277
00:09:45,600 --> 00:09:46,760
I just said it.

278
00:09:47,900 --> 00:09:50,420
(Smiles)

279
00:09:56,150 --> 00:09:57,040
We've paddled enough.

280
00:09:57,320 --> 00:09:57,920
Let's go.

281
00:10:05,080 --> 00:10:06,320
Here, take the blanket.

282
00:10:12,320 --> 00:10:13,240
You can hold onto me.

283
00:10:13,240 --> 00:10:14,400
(Holds on)
Just pull yourself up.

284
00:10:16,240 --> 00:10:17,560
We didn't leave anything, right?

285
00:10:17,560 --> 00:10:18,800
I don't think so.

286
00:10:27,680 --> 00:10:28,080
Let's go.

287
00:10:28,080 --> 00:10:29,320
You're just really tired.

288
00:10:29,960 --> 00:10:31,120
I'm okay. It was fun.

289
00:10:40,240 --> 00:10:41,560
You can sit for a bit.

290
00:10:42,440 --> 00:10:43,680
You haven't used this at all.

291
00:10:44,720 --> 00:10:45,520
This thing.

292
00:10:46,980 --> 00:10:48,520
See if you can get it swinging.

293
00:10:54,120 --> 00:10:55,400
Have you guys tried this before?

294
00:10:55,400 --> 00:10:56,120
Yeah, we tried it.

295
00:10:56,120 --> 00:10:56,800
Why does this feel

296
00:10:56,800 --> 00:10:58,400
more fun than the boat?

297
00:10:58,920 --> 00:11:00,600
I wish they had a two-person swing.

298
00:11:05,680 --> 00:11:06,960
Yeah. Wanna get on?

299
00:11:06,960 --> 00:11:08,600
(Invites)
Try sitting here.

300
00:11:12,900 --> 00:11:14,560
(Walks over)
Can it fit two?

301
00:11:16,480 --> 00:11:17,160
Should be fine.

302
00:11:17,160 --> 00:11:17,520
You first.

303
00:11:17,520 --> 00:11:18,440
(Moves over)
Watch your skirt.

304
00:11:19,260 --> 00:11:20,940
(Sits down)
It really works.

305
00:11:28,880 --> 00:11:29,680
Okay.

306
00:11:30,280 --> 00:11:31,200
I'll move us.

307
00:11:31,200 --> 00:11:32,600
Just keep your feet up.

308
00:11:35,200 --> 00:11:35,480
Wait.

309
00:11:35,480 --> 00:11:36,440
I don't have a good grip.

310
00:11:36,960 --> 00:11:38,520
Let me hold this.

311
00:11:40,160 --> 00:11:40,720
Feet up.

312
00:11:40,720 --> 00:11:41,840
- Okay.
- Feet up.

313
00:11:44,440 --> 00:11:45,480
It really works.

314
00:11:45,480 --> 00:11:46,680
So that's how it works.

315
00:11:49,280 --> 00:11:50,480
This feels wilder than the boat.

316
00:11:50,580 --> 00:11:52,260
(Smiles)

317
00:11:59,640 --> 00:12:01,400
Did you like swings growing up?

318
00:12:01,400 --> 00:12:01,880
Yeah, I did.

319
00:12:01,880 --> 00:12:02,880
I like that

320
00:12:02,880 --> 00:12:04,240
feeling of floating back-and-forth.

321
00:12:05,920 --> 00:12:07,160
But this one swings in a curve,

322
00:12:07,160 --> 00:12:07,960
so it feels different.

323
00:12:17,360 --> 00:12:18,720
Is it lower now?

324
00:12:20,240 --> 00:12:20,760
Okay.

325
00:12:21,360 --> 00:12:21,880
Let's go.

326
00:12:30,480 --> 00:12:32,080
Do you need any seasoning?

327
00:12:32,520 --> 00:12:34,840
Yeah, my Orleans seasoning.

328
00:12:37,100 --> 00:12:38,420
(Sun Bohan's handwritten recipe)

329
00:12:38,520 --> 00:12:39,760
We need flour too, right?

330
00:12:39,760 --> 00:12:40,880
Yeah, flour.

331
00:12:40,900 --> 00:12:42,220
(Scores the chicken)

332
00:12:43,520 --> 00:12:44,960
Just cut it

333
00:12:44,960 --> 00:12:46,320
into thin strips, right?

334
00:12:46,320 --> 00:12:47,580
(Slices ginger)
Yeah, thin strips.

335
00:12:49,360 --> 00:12:51,240
(Concerned)
Watch your hand, Xing.

336
00:12:51,680 --> 00:12:52,480
Okay.

337
00:12:54,340 --> 00:12:55,060
(Glances)

338
00:12:55,620 --> 00:12:56,580
(Glances again)

339
00:12:56,960 --> 00:12:58,080
We don't need this part?

340
00:13:00,160 --> 00:13:00,840
It's fine.

341
00:13:00,840 --> 00:13:01,520
I'm just worried you'll

342
00:13:01,520 --> 00:13:02,680
cut your hand.

343
00:13:04,480 --> 00:13:05,440
That's enough, Xing.

344
00:13:05,440 --> 00:13:06,320
Is this enough?

345
00:13:06,320 --> 00:13:07,120
Yeah, that's enough.

346
00:13:07,120 --> 00:13:07,640
Okay.

347
00:13:09,840 --> 00:13:11,480
Marinate it overnight.

348
00:13:13,120 --> 00:13:15,800
I've actually marinated wings
at home before.

349
00:13:17,440 --> 00:13:18,920
We don't need to do the rest now.

350
00:13:18,920 --> 00:13:20,400
We'll make it all tomorrow.

351
00:13:20,880 --> 00:13:21,400
Okay.

352
00:13:23,440 --> 00:13:24,560
What are you guys doing?

353
00:13:24,560 --> 00:13:25,760
We're marinating wings.

354
00:13:26,360 --> 00:13:27,800
But we can't eat them till tomorrow.

355
00:13:27,800 --> 00:13:28,720
Tomorrow? I see.

356
00:13:28,960 --> 00:13:29,440
Yeah.

357
00:13:29,440 --> 00:13:29,960
Okay.

358
00:13:29,960 --> 00:13:31,280
What did you have for dinner?

359
00:13:31,300 --> 00:13:31,880
(Asks)

360
00:13:31,880 --> 00:13:32,960
We had...

361
00:13:33,320 --> 00:13:34,240
shrimp Cui Yihang made

362
00:13:34,240 --> 00:13:35,040
and pasta.

363
00:13:35,720 --> 00:13:37,040
(Sits up)
Did everyone eat that?

364
00:13:37,400 --> 00:13:38,600
No, just the two of us.

365
00:13:38,600 --> 00:13:39,240
I don't know

366
00:13:39,240 --> 00:13:40,080
what everyone else ate.

367
00:13:40,460 --> 00:13:41,580
(Glances)

368
00:13:46,080 --> 00:13:46,880
Where do you wanna go?

369
00:13:47,600 --> 00:13:49,040
With everyone, or...

370
00:13:50,080 --> 00:13:51,520
I'd rather

371
00:13:51,520 --> 00:13:53,040
have fewer people.

372
00:13:53,040 --> 00:13:53,760
What about you?

373
00:13:56,040 --> 00:13:56,960
Same. Yeah.

374
00:13:59,220 --> 00:14:00,900
(Glances down and smiles)

375
00:14:00,920 --> 00:14:01,840
You're copying me.

376
00:14:02,280 --> 00:14:03,280
You're copying me.

377
00:14:03,280 --> 00:14:04,600
No, just this once.

378
00:14:05,100 --> 00:14:07,340
(Glances)

379
00:14:08,400 --> 00:14:10,560
Next time, you can just say "same" too.

380
00:14:14,320 --> 00:14:15,120
Okay.

381
00:14:18,040 --> 00:14:18,860
From now on, when we ask questions,

382
00:14:18,860 --> 00:14:19,800
we can't give the same answer.

383
00:14:19,800 --> 00:14:20,880
Even if it is the same, don't say it.

384
00:14:20,880 --> 00:14:22,680
You can repeat the answer.

385
00:14:22,680 --> 00:14:24,320
Just don't say "same".

386
00:14:24,320 --> 00:14:25,120
Okay.

387
00:14:27,680 --> 00:14:29,000
They went to the park at midnight?

388
00:14:29,440 --> 00:14:30,680
They stayed at the park till midnight.

389
00:14:31,280 --> 00:14:31,840
I...

390
00:14:31,840 --> 00:14:33,080
I didn't hear them.

391
00:14:33,080 --> 00:14:34,560
(Asks)
Where did you guys go?

392
00:14:34,560 --> 00:14:35,200
We went to...

393
00:14:35,200 --> 00:14:36,080
The park.

394
00:14:36,600 --> 00:14:37,440
Till midnight?

395
00:14:37,500 --> 00:14:39,100
(Asks again)

396
00:14:41,860 --> 00:14:43,580
(Stares)

397
00:14:43,880 --> 00:14:45,160
I heard you were out on the boat

398
00:14:45,160 --> 00:14:46,440
for three or four hours.

399
00:14:46,440 --> 00:14:47,160
That's what they said.

400
00:14:51,200 --> 00:14:52,200
Who said that?

401
00:14:52,300 --> 00:14:53,860
(Plays it cool)

402
00:14:54,240 --> 00:14:54,880
Didn't you?

403
00:14:56,720 --> 00:14:58,200
How long were you out yesterday?

404
00:14:58,200 --> 00:14:59,480
We were out...

405
00:14:59,800 --> 00:15:01,120
not that long.

406
00:15:01,120 --> 00:15:01,680
Yeah.

407
00:15:01,680 --> 00:15:02,560
How long did the

408
00:15:02,560 --> 00:15:03,400
round trip take?

409
00:15:03,400 --> 00:15:04,240
Round trip?

410
00:15:04,240 --> 00:15:04,960
How long were we out?

411
00:15:05,720 --> 00:15:06,680
An hour.

412
00:15:06,680 --> 00:15:07,280
About that.

413
00:15:07,780 --> 00:15:09,300
(Glances)

414
00:15:10,400 --> 00:15:11,360
What are you smiling at?

415
00:15:13,520 --> 00:15:14,800
What are you smiling at?

416
00:15:14,860 --> 00:15:16,580
(Covers mouth)

417
00:15:17,200 --> 00:15:18,000
Nothing.

418
00:15:18,840 --> 00:15:19,960
You two are talking with your eyes.

419
00:15:21,400 --> 00:15:22,120
I... Well,

420
00:15:22,120 --> 00:15:23,840
she's filling me in.

421
00:15:24,240 --> 00:15:24,600
Already?

422
00:15:24,600 --> 00:15:26,000
- It's fine. Sit down.
- She's filling you in already?

423
00:15:27,800 --> 00:15:28,600
What'd she say?

424
00:15:30,280 --> 00:15:32,120
She said she had a great day.

425
00:15:39,360 --> 00:15:40,800
We should use a smaller...

426
00:15:40,800 --> 00:15:41,200
Bowl.

427
00:15:41,200 --> 00:15:42,000
A bowl. Yeah.

428
00:15:44,560 --> 00:15:45,360
Let's go.

429
00:15:45,480 --> 00:15:46,280
Let's go.

430
00:15:50,040 --> 00:15:50,760
How was today?

431
00:15:50,760 --> 00:15:51,760
How'd your exams go?

432
00:15:51,760 --> 00:15:52,600
Pretty well.

433
00:15:53,240 --> 00:15:54,560
Not bad. It wasn't hard.

434
00:15:54,560 --> 00:15:55,360
Today was...

435
00:15:57,080 --> 00:15:57,880
What about today?

436
00:15:58,760 --> 00:16:00,480
Nothing. I'm just saying today was wild.

437
00:16:01,120 --> 00:16:02,120
Why?

438
00:16:02,120 --> 00:16:03,760
I was outside her school.

439
00:16:05,020 --> 00:16:06,700
(Laughs)

440
00:16:08,480 --> 00:16:09,120
What happened?

441
00:16:10,040 --> 00:16:10,800
You got surrounded?

442
00:16:11,160 --> 00:16:11,960
Yeah.

443
00:16:12,440 --> 00:16:13,440
It wasn't that dramatic.

444
00:16:13,440 --> 00:16:16,520
He stood outside
the school with flowers.

445
00:16:16,520 --> 00:16:17,800
So he stood out.

446
00:16:20,200 --> 00:16:22,480
I heard he'd been waiting there a while

447
00:16:22,480 --> 00:16:23,400
before I came out.

448
00:16:25,240 --> 00:16:26,120
So romantic.

449
00:16:27,000 --> 00:16:27,800
Of course.

450
00:16:28,680 --> 00:16:31,000
The Courageous test.

451
00:16:35,640 --> 00:16:36,440
Hey, gorgeous.

452
00:16:37,360 --> 00:16:39,560
The dishwashing crew is official now.

453
00:16:39,880 --> 00:16:40,680
Come sit.

454
00:16:40,680 --> 00:16:41,800
(Gets up)

455
00:16:41,800 --> 00:16:43,080
We can rest a little longer.

456
00:16:43,320 --> 00:16:44,760
Let's rest a bit.

457
00:16:44,880 --> 00:16:45,960
No rush to wash them.

458
00:16:47,880 --> 00:16:50,520
Hide them in that cabinet.

459
00:16:52,360 --> 00:16:54,240
Wash one, then hide the rest.

460
00:16:56,760 --> 00:16:59,360
One for you, one for me.

461
00:17:01,840 --> 00:17:03,120
I'll get the plastic wrap.

462
00:17:06,440 --> 00:17:07,240
Let's do this.

463
00:17:08,200 --> 00:17:09,000
Battle time.

464
00:17:11,119 --> 00:17:14,480
Where's the plastic wrap?

465
00:17:16,980 --> 00:17:18,339
(Glances)

466
00:17:18,359 --> 00:17:21,800
Cao Yiheng keeps sighing as he walks.

467
00:17:21,800 --> 00:17:23,079
No idea why.

468
00:17:24,720 --> 00:17:26,760
He's walking and sighing.

469
00:17:26,760 --> 00:17:27,359
Like this.

470
00:17:30,440 --> 00:17:32,400
I can't find the plastic wrap.

471
00:17:32,400 --> 00:17:35,160
I thought you
were sighing over all the dishes.

472
00:17:37,240 --> 00:17:39,800
Let's make an assembly line, okay?

473
00:17:39,800 --> 00:17:40,880
Sure.

474
00:17:41,480 --> 00:17:42,080
Here it is.

475
00:17:46,520 --> 00:17:47,560
Here, let go.

476
00:17:48,520 --> 00:17:49,400
I'll put it here.

477
00:17:53,200 --> 00:17:55,280
A grateful heart.

478
00:17:56,160 --> 00:17:58,320
Grateful for dishwashing.

479
00:18:00,360 --> 00:18:01,800
I'll put this in the fridge.

480
00:18:01,800 --> 00:18:02,280
Okay.

481
00:18:09,360 --> 00:18:10,160
There's no room.

482
00:18:10,160 --> 00:18:11,200
I need to rinse some first.

483
00:18:11,200 --> 00:18:12,040
I'll do it.

484
00:18:12,040 --> 00:18:12,960
I'll rinse them.

485
00:18:12,960 --> 00:18:13,920
You just...

486
00:18:14,800 --> 00:18:15,400
Don't.

487
00:18:15,400 --> 00:18:16,920
Stay out of the cold water.

488
00:18:17,520 --> 00:18:18,760
It's fine. I can wear gloves.

489
00:18:19,120 --> 00:18:19,800
Seriously.

490
00:18:19,800 --> 00:18:20,240
Don't.

491
00:18:20,240 --> 00:18:21,760
Come on.

492
00:18:23,660 --> 00:18:25,580
(Squeezes)

493
00:18:26,400 --> 00:18:27,200
How about this?

494
00:18:27,200 --> 00:18:29,120
I'll rinse, and you put them away.

495
00:18:30,000 --> 00:18:30,720
Okay?

496
00:18:30,720 --> 00:18:31,400
No.

497
00:18:31,400 --> 00:18:32,560
It's okay.

498
00:18:33,980 --> 00:18:35,860
(Stares)

499
00:18:36,480 --> 00:18:37,560
Three.

500
00:18:37,560 --> 00:18:38,120
Two.

501
00:18:39,600 --> 00:18:41,200
Don't pull that on me.

502
00:18:41,200 --> 00:18:41,680
Just leave it.

503
00:18:41,680 --> 00:18:43,120
How about I get you some hot water?

504
00:18:43,120 --> 00:18:43,480
Okay.

505
00:18:43,480 --> 00:18:44,200
Is there hot water?

506
00:18:44,200 --> 00:18:44,720
Yeah.

507
00:18:59,840 --> 00:19:00,760
Almost done?

508
00:19:02,160 --> 00:19:03,600
Nice.

509
00:19:03,600 --> 00:19:04,600
I'll start drying dishes.

510
00:19:12,520 --> 00:19:14,560
It's fine. Pass me some
when you're halfway.

511
00:19:15,760 --> 00:19:17,440
So we can dry them twice?

512
00:19:17,440 --> 00:19:18,640
Let's go fast first.

513
00:19:19,240 --> 00:19:20,320
Gotta be fast.

514
00:19:20,320 --> 00:19:20,880
Pick up the pace.

515
00:19:20,880 --> 00:19:22,080
We've got an assembly line now.

516
00:19:22,080 --> 00:19:22,600
Yep.

517
00:19:22,600 --> 00:19:23,480
Take it.

518
00:19:23,480 --> 00:19:24,320
Assembly line.

519
00:19:24,320 --> 00:19:26,080
Take it. Hurry.

520
00:19:26,080 --> 00:19:26,400
Here.

521
00:19:27,560 --> 00:19:28,920
Keep it moving.

522
00:19:28,920 --> 00:19:29,560
Nice rhythm.

523
00:19:31,280 --> 00:19:33,560
We've got the rhythm now.

524
00:19:33,560 --> 00:19:35,280
Things are heating up over here.

525
00:19:36,560 --> 00:19:37,640
We're on fire.

526
00:19:44,860 --> 00:19:45,700
(Unique Dream of Red Mansion)

527
00:19:45,720 --> 00:19:46,880
Okay, you can take off

528
00:19:46,880 --> 00:19:47,760
your blindfold now.

529
00:20:04,520 --> 00:20:05,280
Okay.

530
00:20:12,480 --> 00:20:13,720
There's one little impression too.

531
00:20:13,720 --> 00:20:15,880
You need to imitate

532
00:20:15,880 --> 00:20:17,000
anyone you want.

533
00:20:17,000 --> 00:20:17,920
You can imitate

534
00:20:17,920 --> 00:20:18,840
something they always say

535
00:20:18,840 --> 00:20:20,080
or a gesture they always do.

536
00:20:20,080 --> 00:20:20,920
Anything works.

537
00:20:20,920 --> 00:20:22,360
But don't say who it is.

538
00:20:22,920 --> 00:20:23,800
Just let everyone guess.

539
00:20:24,280 --> 00:20:25,680
I need a chair.

540
00:20:27,440 --> 00:20:29,120
Now we already know.

541
00:20:29,640 --> 00:20:31,200
The chair gave it away?

542
00:20:31,720 --> 00:20:32,960
We already have the answer.

543
00:20:33,760 --> 00:20:35,480
Alright, let's see this impression.

544
00:20:36,880 --> 00:20:37,920
Three, two, one.

545
00:20:45,040 --> 00:20:46,360
(Glances)
How do you guys lean back like that?

546
00:20:47,000 --> 00:20:47,920
How do you lean back like that?

547
00:20:47,920 --> 00:20:49,480
Why is it so uncomfortable when I do it?

548
00:20:49,480 --> 00:20:50,500
(Leans back)

549
00:20:51,000 --> 00:20:52,200
No, I've always wanted to ask Sun Bohan

550
00:20:52,200 --> 00:20:53,400
how he always

551
00:20:53,400 --> 00:20:54,760
looks so relaxed leaning back.

552
00:20:55,040 --> 00:20:56,560
I just think...

553
00:20:57,280 --> 00:20:58,560
whatever's comfortable works.

554
00:21:08,040 --> 00:21:09,560
I'm gonna do my impression now.

555
00:21:09,560 --> 00:21:10,960
Okay, I'll get you a chair?

556
00:21:12,640 --> 00:21:13,880
Sir, I don't need a chair.

557
00:21:13,880 --> 00:21:14,400
Okay.

558
00:21:14,840 --> 00:21:16,160
But now I'm not sure

559
00:21:16,160 --> 00:21:18,200
who I'm imitating.

560
00:21:21,640 --> 00:21:23,640
They both do this.

561
00:21:33,560 --> 00:21:34,680
That's how they talk?

562
00:21:34,680 --> 00:21:35,160
What do you mean?

563
00:21:35,160 --> 00:21:36,280
These two always

564
00:21:36,280 --> 00:21:37,320
do this?

565
00:21:39,720 --> 00:21:40,480
And then this?

566
00:21:40,480 --> 00:21:41,720
Left and right.

567
00:21:41,720 --> 00:21:42,560
Together?

568
00:21:42,560 --> 00:21:44,720
Yeah, they both do this.

569
00:21:44,720 --> 00:21:45,680
Like this?

570
00:21:46,040 --> 00:21:47,200
Which two are they?

571
00:21:47,580 --> 00:21:48,460
(Glances right)

572
00:21:48,460 --> 00:21:49,060
(Glances left)

573
00:21:49,280 --> 00:21:50,600
Si and Xing.

574
00:21:50,600 --> 00:21:52,320
They always do this when they talk.

575
00:21:52,320 --> 00:21:53,640
Yeah, so now I don't know

576
00:21:53,640 --> 00:21:54,400
which one I'm doing.

577
00:21:55,520 --> 00:21:56,160
We do this?

578
00:21:56,800 --> 00:21:57,600
Like this.

579
00:22:05,640 --> 00:22:06,440
You know what?

580
00:22:07,120 --> 00:22:08,080
It's actually true.

581
00:22:10,840 --> 00:22:12,440
So why do you

582
00:22:12,440 --> 00:22:13,400
always do that?

583
00:22:13,400 --> 00:22:15,400
Are you holding a mic or something?

584
00:22:15,400 --> 00:22:16,800
Because I speak pretty softly.

585
00:22:16,800 --> 00:22:18,480
(Joking)
I keep a mic in my hand.

586
00:22:26,360 --> 00:22:27,800
What about you?

587
00:22:27,800 --> 00:22:29,360
You speak pretty softly too?

588
00:22:29,960 --> 00:22:32,360
Yeah, so I've got
two microphones in here.

589
00:22:34,100 --> 00:22:35,220
(Teases)

590
00:22:38,040 --> 00:22:39,280
Two microphones in here.

591
00:22:39,280 --> 00:22:40,120
Who?

592
00:22:40,440 --> 00:22:41,240
Me...

593
00:22:41,720 --> 00:22:43,200
(Teases)
Just leave it by the door.

594
00:22:43,400 --> 00:22:44,040
Okay.

595
00:22:48,200 --> 00:22:49,240
So next,

596
00:22:49,240 --> 00:22:52,760
who'll walk to the center of the court?

597
00:22:52,760 --> 00:22:55,560
Three, two, one. Go!

598
00:22:56,740 --> 00:22:58,220
(Sun Qimeng steps forward)

599
00:22:59,040 --> 00:23:01,780
Now, the four guys,

600
00:23:01,780 --> 00:23:03,460
(Zhao Xilun steps forward)
step forward bravely.

601
00:23:03,460 --> 00:23:04,620
(Chen Hewen steps forward)

602
00:23:05,180 --> 00:23:06,140
(Sun Bohan steps forward)

603
00:23:06,420 --> 00:23:07,720
(Cui Yihang steps forward)
Good. Nice.

604
00:23:09,120 --> 00:23:10,280
Alright, let's begin!

605
00:23:11,080 --> 00:23:11,760
Meng!

606
00:23:12,880 --> 00:23:15,440
You're such an energetic person.

607
00:23:15,640 --> 00:23:16,720
Every day,

608
00:23:16,720 --> 00:23:18,400
you always say you're the last one back,

609
00:23:18,400 --> 00:23:19,760
but we all know

610
00:23:19,760 --> 00:23:21,440
you're the busiest and most exhausted.

611
00:23:21,680 --> 00:23:24,400
You're also really thoughtful
and caring.

612
00:23:24,400 --> 00:23:26,680
I think you're brave and sincere.

613
00:23:26,680 --> 00:23:27,720
I'm glad I met you.

614
00:23:41,080 --> 00:23:41,880
Meng!

615
00:23:44,480 --> 00:23:46,600
I feel like you're someone

616
00:23:46,600 --> 00:23:47,800
who really knows how to care for others.

617
00:23:48,280 --> 00:23:49,640
I hope you'll always be happy

618
00:23:49,640 --> 00:23:51,680
and bravely make your own choices.

619
00:23:56,920 --> 00:23:57,800
Meng!

620
00:23:58,280 --> 00:24:00,640
I hope that while you're here,

621
00:24:00,960 --> 00:24:02,240
you'll bravely be yourself.

622
00:24:03,280 --> 00:24:04,200
From what I've seen,

623
00:24:04,200 --> 00:24:06,720
you're warm and outgoing.

624
00:24:06,720 --> 00:24:08,600
I hope you'll take better care
of your feelings

625
00:24:09,400 --> 00:24:11,040
and don't do anything you'll regret.

626
00:24:11,040 --> 00:24:11,800
Be brave.

627
00:24:13,000 --> 00:24:14,080
Okay.

628
00:24:14,400 --> 00:24:16,000
That's so sweet. I'm gonna cry.

629
00:24:18,680 --> 00:24:19,840
Don't cry.

630
00:24:19,840 --> 00:24:20,800
Happy tears.

631
00:24:20,800 --> 00:24:21,520
Yeah, really.

632
00:24:23,280 --> 00:24:23,800
Meng.

633
00:24:25,360 --> 00:24:27,440
I feel like you're

634
00:24:27,440 --> 00:24:28,920
a really thoughtful person.

635
00:24:29,400 --> 00:24:30,120
You're positive,

636
00:24:30,120 --> 00:24:31,520
bright, and cheerful.

637
00:24:31,520 --> 00:24:34,720
I hope you stay cheerful and positive

638
00:24:34,880 --> 00:24:36,120
and keep spreading that energy.

639
00:24:36,400 --> 00:24:38,640
I hope you're always happy.

640
00:24:38,960 --> 00:24:39,880
Thank you.

641
00:24:45,160 --> 00:24:47,480
This is a beautiful dream,

642
00:24:47,920 --> 00:24:48,720
but

643
00:24:49,200 --> 00:24:52,000
it's also our real life.

644
00:24:55,560 --> 00:24:57,320
Everyone, let's

645
00:24:57,660 --> 00:25:00,580
be brave enough to love!

646
00:25:16,220 --> 00:25:18,940
"♪Morning steam rises
from breakfast stalls♪

647
00:25:18,940 --> 00:25:21,540
♪Packed subway cars,
barely room to breathe♪

648
00:25:21,540 --> 00:25:25,740
♪Still half asleep, another day begins♪

649
00:25:26,900 --> 00:25:29,620
♪The city glows beneath the towers♪

650
00:25:29,620 --> 00:25:32,260
♪Somewhere beyond the clouds,
a sweet little date awaits♪

651
00:25:32,260 --> 00:25:36,340
♪But first,
there are endless meetings to survive♪

652
00:25:37,060 --> 00:25:38,460
♪Even if the fairy tale
only lasts a day♪

653
00:25:38,460 --> 00:25:39,780
♪I'll still give it everything I have♪

654
00:25:39,780 --> 00:25:41,100
♪Love out loud♪

655
00:25:41,100 --> 00:25:42,500
♪Don't let this summer slip away♪

656
00:25:42,500 --> 00:25:43,740
♪Cupid's arrow is already on its way♪

657
00:25:43,740 --> 00:25:45,140
♪Don't act like you didn't see it♪

658
00:25:45,140 --> 00:25:48,100
♪Just be a little braver♪

659
00:25:48,100 --> 00:25:49,340
♪Keep moving♪

660
00:25:49,460 --> 00:25:50,940
♪Keep moving♪

661
00:25:50,940 --> 00:25:54,300
♪There's a little spark shining
in your eyes♪

662
00:25:56,660 --> 00:25:59,020
♪That's the signal
of a heart coming alive♪

663
00:26:09,460 --> 00:26:12,260
♪Keep moving♪

664
00:26:12,260 --> 00:26:14,900
♪Life can be complicated,
yet beautifully simple♪

665
00:26:14,900 --> 00:26:17,540
♪Go discover♪

666
00:26:17,540 --> 00:26:20,220
♪That heartbeat you've been longing
to let out♪

667
00:26:20,220 --> 00:26:22,900
♪Come closer♪

668
00:26:22,900 --> 00:26:26,300
♪There's a little spark shining
in your eyes♪

669
00:26:28,740 --> 00:26:31,540
♪That's the signal
of a heart coming alive♪"
